  "rules_sha256": "74e4e0eae1e5ec54bca0b9926a8b0cf9d6a973115371e4df4351599bf188dc6a",
  "scope": "All integer contact heights 4..156 and all legal contact offsets, paddle bounds 15..145, speed 2, exact rounding/wall/contact order; initial standard serves. Safe defense is a diagnostic scripted construction, not a learned competition submission.",
  "inductive_argument": [
    "Standard serves and all future legal physics states have integer coordinates and velocities; the enumeration covers a superset of all reachable legal contact heights and offsets.",
    "For each opponent contact height, the universal safe band contains exactly the starting paddle centers from which every legal returned shot can be caught. Exact movement reachability includes staying, two-unit motion, clamping, and clamp-then-reverse paths.",
    "The incoming greedy chase catches every legal shot from every safe-band integer start. Its landing prediction is invariant during that flight.",
    "After any legal return, the hitter can move into the safe band corresponding to the known next contact height before the opponent hits. The strict nearest-band movement rule achieves this for every enumerated return, with both players moving on each intervening tick.",
    "Both first-serve roles satisfy the base case: the receiver catches the serve, while the other player reaches the safe band before the first return.",
    "By induction, either player can avoid every miss against any sequence of legal opponent actions from a standard serve. Timeout and valid loop exits may draw, but cannot create a conceded point."
  ]
